Subject: dxgi: make DComp window teardown complete, idempotent and owning-thread

Releasing a swapchain from a thread other than its target window's
skipped every window-owning cleanup: the reblit timers kept firing, the
subclass stayed installed, the composition properties leaked, and the
subclassed-target count never fell, so winex11 kept classifying
ownerless tool popups as menus for the rest of the session. A
same-thread release also left the popup-stack entry, the desktop active
property and the parent clip bit behind, and a release followed by
window destruction could tear down twice.

Factor the whole teardown into dcomp_teardown_window: timers, subclass
restore with ownership validation, all composition properties, the
popup-stack entry, the active count and the parent clip, one-shot via a
__wine_dcomp_subclassed marker. Both NCDESTROY handlers, same-thread
release and a new WM_WINE_DCOMP_TEARDOWN message use it; a cross-thread
release posts that message to the owning thread instead of skipping,
and the comp window destroy marshals the same way.
WINE_DCOMP_TEARDOWN=legacy restores the old release path for
comparison.

